{0 Ptools}


[Ptools] refers to the toolchain for [PISA], [PASM], [PHDL], etc.


{1 The tools}

Find the documentation for the tools here:

- {{:../assembler/index.html} Assembler}: Assembles [PASM] programs into intermediate [PASM] programs (resolved labels, base instructions only), or ASCII representations of [PISA] binaries, or actual [PISA] binaries.

- {{:../disassembler/index.html} Disassembler}: Disassembles [PISA] binaries to basic [PASM] programs.

- {{:../cpu-simulator/index.html} CPU simulator}: An ISA simulator to simulate the execution of [PISA] programs on a [PISA] processor. Shows the final processor state, the instruction-by-instruction traces and has a debug mode.

- {{:../ram-init/index.html} RAM Init}: Initializes RAM images from a textual description of the RAM. Meant to be used to generate initial RAM images to feed the CPU simulator.

- {{:../hdl-simulator/index.html} HDL simulator}: Simulating circuits described using [PHDL].


{1 Installation}

The [build.sh] script can be used to build all the executables (using [dune build]). It places them all in the [executables] directory. Add it to your [PATH] to invoke the executables from any directory.

{v
λ:~/ptools⟩ ./build.sh 
Buliding executables...
Assembler        :    Build successful.
Disassembler     :    Build successful.
CPU simulator    :    Build successful.
RAM Init         :    Build successful.
HDL simulator    :    Build successful.
Building successful. Placing executables in ./executables
Script executed.

λ:~/ptools⟩ ls -l executables
assembler
cpusim
dis
hdl-simulator
ram-init
v}


{1 Source code}

The source code for all of the tools can be viewd on our {{:https://gitlab.com/verify-at-iitpkd/focs/ptools} GitLab repository}.

